  "title": "No connection with STM32U5 after unchecked nSWBOOT0 in option bytes",
  "content": "<p>Hello,</p><p>I’m working on STM32U5 flash with tfm application using script “regression.sh” and “TFM_UPDATE.sh” of MB1551 example project in SBSFU. I lost the connection with the chip when I unchecked nSWBOOT0 in option bytes.</p><p>Trust Zone : activated</p><p>nBoot0 : checked</p><p>nSWBOOT0 : unchecked</p><p>RDP : 0</p><p> </p><p>So when we try a JTAG connection, we have this error.</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/cd82c738-75f9-43c8-836b-4a7ede7d6f50.png\" /><figcaption>STM32CubeProgrammer Error connection</figcaption></figure><p> </p><p>Do you know a solution to regain connection with the STM32U5 ?</p><p>Thanks for your attention,</p><p>Kind regards,</p>",
